## 2. Extend `FieldDef` with the field types deep customization actually needs

Add these variants to the `FieldDef` union in `mock/layers.ts`. Keep all 7 existing variants exactly as they are — this is additive.

```
| { key: string; label: string; type: 'model-select'; value: ModelSelection; help?: string }
| { key: string; label: string; type: 'prompt'; value: string; variables?: string[]; help?: string }
| { key: string; label: string; type: 'code'; language?: 'json' | 'python' | 'javascript'; value: string; help?: string }
| { key: string; label: string; type: 'json'; value: string; help?: string }
| { key: string; label: string; type: 'key-value'; value: { key: string; value: string }[]; help?: string }
| { key: string; label: string; type: 'weighted-list'; options: string[]; value: Record<string, number>; help?: string }
| { key: string; label: string; type: 'credential'; provider?: string; value: string; help?: string }
| { key: string; label: string; type: 'dataset-ref'; value: string | null; help?: string }
```

Where `ModelSelection` (new type, define alongside `FieldDef`) is:
```
interface ModelSelection {
  providerId: string          // 'openai' | 'anthropic' | 'google' | 'alibaba' | 'deepseek' | 'ollama' | ...
  modelId: string             // e.g. 'gpt-5', or the free-typed model tag for ollama, e.g. 'llama3.1:8b'
  endpoint?: string           // only meaningful for 'ollama' — defaults to http://localhost:11434
  temperature: number
  maxTokens: number
}
```

Notes on each new type's purpose, so the agent implementing this understands what it's for and doesn't render something generic:
- **`model-select`**: the model/provider picker itself — see §3, it's a dedicated composite control, not a plain `Select`.
- **`prompt`**: a multi-line system/instruction prompt. `variables` lists the `{{variable}}` tokens this node's actual wired inputs make available (computed at render time from the node's real incoming edges, not hardcoded on the `ComponentDef` — see §5) so the editor can offer an "insert variable" affordance.
- **`code`**: free-form code for things like a custom scoring function or a custom risk rule — render as a monospace `Textarea` with a visible line-number gutter (a simple CSS `counter-reset`/`counter-increment` on wrapped `<div>`s per line is enough; don't pull in a full code-editor dependency like Monaco or CodeMirror for this, it's disproportionate to what these fields need). No execution, ever — this is captured as a string, never run client-side.
- **`json`**: raw structured config for power users (e.g., a custom webhook payload template) — monospace `Textarea`, validated as parseable JSON on blur, with an inline error message if it doesn't parse (don't block typing, just don't accept an invalid save — mirror how `password`/`text` fields already show a `help` line, reuse that slot for the error state).
- **`key-value`**: dynamic add/remove list of string pairs (e.g., custom HTTP headers for a data feed). Render as repeated two-`Input` rows with a trailing remove `X` button and a "+ Add row" button below — this exact repeated-row-with-remove pattern doesn't exist elsewhere in the codebase yet, so build it once as its own small subcomponent.
- **`weighted-list`**: N sliders that share a "should roughly sum to 100" relationship (e.g., debate-layer agent weighting, ensemble blend weights) — render as N `SliderWithValue`s, and show a running total at the bottom with a color cue (`text-profit` at ~100, `text-warn` otherwise) — don't hard-block saving at an imperfect sum, just make the imbalance visible.
- **`credential`**: like `password`, but with a "Test connection" button next to it that does a fake 900ms delay then shows a green check or a red X (randomly succeed unless the field is empty, in which case always fail) — this is for things like a broker API key or a custom data-provider key where "does this even look valid" matters more than the raw secret.
- **`dataset-ref`**: a reference to an uploaded dataset. Since there's no real file upload in this app, render this as a `Select` populated from a small new mock list (`MOCK_DATASETS` in `mock/data.ts` — 4–5 fake entries: name, row count, date range, size) plus a "browse for more" state that's clearly a placeholder (a disabled "Upload custom dataset (coming soon)" row at the bottom of the list) — real file upload is out of scope for all four phases.

Update `defaultConfig()` and `computeNeedsConfig()` in `lib/workspace-store.ts` to handle every new type:
- `defaultConfig`: use each field's `value` as-is for all new types except `model-select`, which needs a real default (pick the first provider's first model, `temperature: 0.7`, `maxTokens: 1024`).
- `computeNeedsConfig`: extend the "still blank" check to also cover `model-select` (empty `modelId`), `credential` (empty `value`), and `dataset-ref` (`null` value) — these are exactly as "must be filled before this node can run" as the existing `text`/`password` check.

