`app/app/settings/page.tsx` currently has "NSE Realtime Datafeed Key" and "Broker Execution API Key" as flat text fields on a general settings page, with help text literally saying *"Used by OHLCV and Orderbook feeds in Layer I"* and *"Used for paper and live order placement in Layer IX"* — these keys belong on the nodes that use them, not on an unrelated global settings page. Once `credential`-type `advancedFields` exist on `ohlcv-feed`/`orderbook-depth` (Layer I) and the paper/live execution nodes (Layer IX), remove these two fields from the Settings page entirely (they're superseded, not duplicated — a key belongs in exactly one place) and add a short note where they used to be: "Market data and broker credentials now live on their respective nodes in the Builder — open any Data or Execution node's Deep Customization panel." If you're running this phase before or without Phase 5's Account section, this note lives on the current flat `/app/settings` page; if Phase 5 already moved things to `/app/account/profile`, put the note there instead.

