## 8. Backward compatibility — don't let this phase break every already-saved bot

Every bot already saved (the seeded mock bots, and anything a real user built before this phase shipped) has `node.config` objects keyed only to the *old* `fields` list. The moment you add `advancedFields` with new keys to a `ComponentDef`, every existing saved node is missing those keys in its stored `config`.

Fix this once, centrally: wherever a bot's graph is loaded into the builder (`load` in `lib/builder-store.ts`, called from `builder/[botId]/page.tsx`), merge each node's stored `config` on top of `defaultConfig(comp)` instead of using the stored `config` as-is:
```
const comp = COMPONENT_MAP[node.componentId]
const mergedConfig = comp ? { ...defaultConfig(comp), ...node.config } : node.config
```
This guarantees every field this component definition now expects has *some* value (the default) even for a bot that was saved before that field existed, while never clobbering a value the user actually set. Do this in Phase 6, even though the deeper storage/versioning rework is Phase 7 — an old bot silently missing half its config the first time someone opens it after this update would be a bad regression to ship.

